## § 7. VERSION SOVEREIGNTY COMMANDS (Auto-Sync System)

```bash
dv version-scan      # Read-only: show all stale version strings fleet-wide
dv nuke-versions     # Fix all stale strings, auto-commit + push per project
dv version:bump X.Y.Z # Atomic version bump across all config files
dv rules             # Broadcast .cursorrules + auto-runs nuke-versions
```

**Machine Law**: `dv nuke-versions` runs automatically at the end of every `dv rules` broadcast.
Every future fleet sync will auto-correct any version drift that has accumulated.
You can also run `dv version-scan` at any time to audit without making changes.

### Version Bump Procedure (v8.4.0 → v8.5.0)
1. `dv version:bump 8.5.0` — atomically bumps all version files
2. `dv nuke-versions` — purges residual old strings fleet-wide (auto-commits + pushes)
3. `git push origin master --no-verify`
4. `dv rules` — broadcasts + runs nuke-versions automatically
5. On all other machines: `git pull --rebase origin master && dv nuke-versions`

## 8. SESSION-START TEST REGISTRY PROTOCOL

At the start of every Infinity Protocol session, run:

```bash
dv test-manifest:show    # Verify globalFloor and per-file floors
dv version-scan          # Confirm fleet has no stale version strings
```

If `globalFloor` is more than 15% below the actual test count shown by `npm run test:unit`:
```bash
dv test-manifest:update  # Recalculates floor from live test run, auto-commits
```

**Machine Law**: Every session touching a protocol project MUST run `dv test-manifest:show` before making changes. A floor below 85% of actual tests is a protocol breach.

