## § 9. CANARY DEPLOYMENT VERIFICATION

After any protocol upgrade, verify the new rules are active before marking the upgrade complete:

```bash
# Verify the upgraded rule is active in a canary project
TARGET_PROJECT="azdj-academy"
EXPECTED="v8.4.0"
ACTUAL=$(grep -m1 "Infinity Protocol" "$HOME/Developer/$TARGET_PROJECT/.cursorrules" | grep -oE "v[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+")
if [ "$ACTUAL" = "$EXPECTED" ]; then
  echo "✓ Canary PASS: $TARGET_PROJECT on $ACTUAL"
else
  echo "✗ Canary FAIL: $TARGET_PROJECT shows $ACTUAL — run dv rules"
  exit 1
fi
```

Run this check against a minimum of 3 projects after every `dv rules` broadcast. If any canary fails: halt deployment, investigate, re-broadcast.

